# NEARS-2460 — AC1 could not be demonstrated: login blocked before Menu is reachable

## Live device log (VendorApp, emulator-5554, com.izzes.nearsvendor pid 23894)
08-26 08:20:46.219 23894 23894 I flutter : [FAIL] endpoint=/api/v1/auth/vendor/login http_status=401 type=ApiFailure msg="unhandled api response" correlation_id=595c83a0-53ce-4195-930c-48a3c060c6f8
08-26 08:22:49.198 23894 23894 I flutter : [FAIL] endpoint=/api/v1/auth/vendor/login http_status=401 type=ApiFailure msg="unhandled api response" correlation_id=45d471d3-ea70-4db0-a6b4-f2351076d946

Login attempted twice via the live UI (fastmarket@demo.com / 123456789, Vendor Owner tab) —
both attempts 401. Server response shown to the user via showCustomSnackBar(status.message)
(VendorApp/lib/features/auth/screens/sign_in_screen.dart:246) — not a silent failure, but a
DIFFERENT gate than AC1 describes.

## Direct backend reproduction (same local backend, same credentials, vendor_type=owner)
$ curl -s -X POST http://127.0.0.1:8000/api/v1/auth/vendor/login -H "Content-Type: application/json" \
    -d '{"email":"fastmarket@demo.com","password":"123456789","vendor_type":"owner"}'
{"errors":[{"code":"no_mobile_app","message":"Your Subscription Plan is not Active for Mobile App"}]}

Password hash independently confirmed correct (read-only): Hash::check('123456789', vendor 18's
password) => MATCH. So this is NOT a bad-credentials 401 — it is VendorLoginController's
storeSubscriptionCheck() gate at Admin/app/Http/Controllers/Api/V1/Auth/VendorLoginController.php:355-370:

    if ($store?->store_business_model == 'subscription') {
        $store_sub = $store?->store_sub;
        if (isset($store_sub)) {
            if ($store_sub?->mobile_app == 0) {
                return [...'code' => 401, 'errors' => [['code' => 'no_mobile_app', ...]]];
            }
        }
    }

## DB read (read-only, no mutation)
mysql> SELECT id,store_id,package_id,expiry_date,status,mobile_app,pos,chat,review,self_delivery,is_trial
       FROM store_subscriptions WHERE store_id=21;
+----+----------+------------+-------------+--------+------------+-----+------+--------+---------------+----------+
| id | store_id | package_id | expiry_date | status | mobile_app | pos | chat | review | self_delivery | is_trial |
+----+----------+------------+-------------+--------+------------+-----+------+--------+---------------+----------+
|  1 |       21 |          1 | 2031-08-26  |      1 |          0 |   0 |    0 |      0 |             0 |        0 |
+----+----------+------------+-------------+--------+------------+-----+------+--------+---------------+----------+

status=1 and expiry_date=2031-08-26 are exactly as the ticket describes ("healthy"), but
mobile_app=0 — a field the seeder's ensureSubscription() never sets, on EITHER the insert path
(Admin/database/seeders/StorePanelIdorQaFixtureSeeder.php:117-133, no 'mobile_app' key => column
DEFAULT 0) or the stale-update path (only expiry_date/status/updated_at are touched). The login
gate above checks mobile_app independently of status/expiry_date, so it blocks the vendor before
the app ever reaches the dashboard/Menu tab where the client-side gate this ticket targets
(SubscriptionController.trialEndBottomSheet(), which reads profile.subscription.status) would
even run.

## Consequence for AC1
AC1 ("the 'Your Package is Expired' bottom sheet does NOT appear and Menu screens are
reachable") cannot be demonstrated PASS or FAIL on its own terms — the vendor cannot sign in at
all, so Menu is categorically unreachable. This is a worse failure mode than the one the ticket
set out to fix.

## Regression check (store 19 / vendor 16, commission model — unaffected)
$ curl -s -X POST http://127.0.0.1:8000/api/v1/auth/vendor/login -H "Content-Type: application/json" \
    -d '{"email":"ecomarket@demo.com","password":"123456789","vendor_type":"owner"}'
{"token":"...","zone_wise_topic":null,"store_id":19,"module_type":"grocery"}

Commission-model stores skip the store_business_model=='subscription' branch entirely
(VendorLoginController.php:355), so store 19 logs in normally — confirms the regression guard
holds; the mobile_app gap is scoped to store 21's subscription row only.
